---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Cookies" description="The cookies the Access:Hull website uses, and how to change your cookie settings.">

  <section class="ah-sec" aria-labelledby="ck-h"><div class="ah-in lg-wrap">
    <nav class="lg-nav" aria-label="Policies"><a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility statement</a><a href="/privacy/">Privacy notice</a><a href="/cookies/" aria-current="page">Cookies</a><a href="/terms/">Terms of use</a></nav>
    <article class="lg">
      <p class="ah-eyebrow">Policies</p>
      <h1 id="ck-h">Cookies</h1>
      <p class="lg-up">Last updated 2 October 2026</p>
      <p class="lg-lead">Cookies are small files saved on your phone, tablet or computer when you visit a website. This page explains how Access:Hull uses them.</p>

      <h2>Cookies we use</h2>
      <p>We don't use advertising cookies, and we don't track you across other websites.</p>
      <div class="tscroll"><table class="lg-t">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">Do we use it?</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Essential</td><td>Keeps the site working, for example remembering your cookie choices (<code>ah-consent</code>, kept for 12 months) and letting you send forms securely</td><td>Yes. These can't be turned off.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Remember my settings</td><td>Remembers the last postcode you searched and the ward you chose (<code>ah-prefs</code>), only on your device</td><td>Only if you turn it on</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Analytics</td><td>Counts visits and shows which pages are used, so we can improve the site</td><td>We don't run any analytics tools yet. If we add one, it will only run if you've said yes.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Marketing</td><td>Tracks you across websites to show adverts</td><td>No, never.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>This site loads its typeface, Montserrat, from Google Fonts. Google receives your device's IP address when the font loads, but doesn't set cookies for this.</p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>Some pages link to other websites, such as Ofcom or mobile networks. Those sites have their own cookie policies.</p>

      <h2>Your cookie settings</h2>
      <div class="ck-status-box"><p id="ck-status" aria-live="polite"></p><button type="button" class="btn btn-p" data-ck="open">Change cookie settings</button></div>
      <p>We ask again every 12 months, or sooner if we change how we use cookies. If you turn off "Remember my settings", we delete what we saved straight away.</p>

      <h2>Managing cookies in your browser</h2>
      <p>You can also delete or block cookies in your browser settings. If you block essential cookies, some parts of the site, such as the forms, may not work.</p>
      <p>Questions? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div></section>

</Base>
